<h3>Transportation</h3>
<p>Getting around the Silk Road is where many travelers underestimate costs. Distances are vast — Urumqi to Kashgar is 1,500km, and the drive takes 20+ hours.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Private vehicle with driver:</strong> $120 – $200 per day (includes fuel, tolls, driver)</li>
  <li><strong>Domestic flights (China):</strong> $80 – $250 one way (Urumqi–Xi'an, Urumqi–Kashgar)</li>
  <li><strong>High-speed train:</strong> $30 – $80 (Lanzhou–Dunhuang, Xi'an–Lanzhou)</li>
  <li><strong>Overnight train (soft sleeper):</strong> $50 – $100 (Urumqi–Kashgar, Xi'an–Urumqi)</li>
  <li><strong>Central Asia border crossings:</strong> $50 – $150 (shared taxi or private transfer)</li>
</ul>

<h3>Guides</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>English-speaking local guide:</strong> $80 – $150 per day</li>
  <li><strong>Spanish/French/German guide:</strong> $120 – $200 per day (limited availability)</li>
  <li><strong>Group tour guide (shared):</strong> $15 – $30 per person per day</li>
</ul>

<h3>Food</h3>
<p>Food is one of the best values along the Silk Road. Street food and local restaurants offer incredible flavors at low prices.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Budget (street food, local eateries):</strong> $10 – $20 per day</li>
  <li><strong>Mid-range (restaurants, hotel breakfast):</strong> $25 – $50 per day</li>
  <li><strong>Luxury (fine dining, hotel restaurants):</strong> $60 – $150 per day</li>
</ul>

<h3>Entrance Fees & Activities</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Mogao Caves (Dunhuang):</strong> $35 – $55</li>
  <li><strong>Jiayuguan Fortress:</strong> $15 – $20</li>
  <li><strong>Zhangye Danxia National Park:</strong> $10 – $15</li>
  <li><strong>Potala Palace (Lhasa):</strong> $15 – $30 (timed entry)</li>
  <li><strong>Camel ride (Dunhuang):</strong> $15 – $25</li>
  <li><strong>Hot air balloon (Turpan):</strong> $150 – $250</li>
  <li><strong>Total average for 7-day tour:</strong> $150 – $300 per person</li>
</ul>

<h3>Permits & Visas</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Chinese tourist visa (L visa):</strong> $140 – $180 (US citizens), $50 – $100 (other nationalities)</li>
  <li><strong>Tibet travel permit:</strong> $30 – $50 (required for all foreign travelers, must be arranged by tour operator)</li>
  <li><strong>Xinjiang border permits:</strong> $15 – $30 (for areas near Pakistan, Kazakhstan borders)</li>
  <li><strong>Uzbekistan e-visa:</strong> $20 – $50</li>
  <li><strong>Kyrgyzstan e-visa:</strong> $40 – $70</li>
  <li><strong>Kazakhstan visa-free:</strong> Free for 30 days (many nationalities)</li>
</ul>

